I look at my computer.
I miss my home in Mexico a little bit.
"I would like to see your house, dad," I say.
My dad smiles at me.
He goes outside with the phone.
I can see a large garden.
The sun is shining a lot there.
"Look, Maya," my dad says.
"Here is a house and a tree."
It is a very big tree.
It is a beautiful tree.
I smile at my screen.
I feel good and warm inside.
My mother, my sister, and my brother come outside too.
My dog runs under the tree.
My whole family waves at me.
"Goodbye, my family!" I say.
"Goodbye, Maya," they say.
I close my computer.
